        "id": 1097542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-16T17:26:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only way to not defer deletion is to block the worker thread until any writes have completed.  If that works for your scenario, we can remove deferred deletion. \n I\u0027d rather not make the worker thread so complex that we remove tasks from it.\n \nIf you have any tests we could add to showcase problems, I think that would help quite a lot in supporting your use case without breaking others.",
      "parentUuid": "4ee01b37_5d008e8f",
      "revId": "694bfc703e12caf62b348924c4c45f742ec66db6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d8435e0_78e2a039",
        "filename": "opengl/libs/EGL/MultifileBlobCache.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 364,
      "author": {
        "id": 2028338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-16T18:24:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The only way to not defer deletion is to block the worker thread until \nany writes have completed.\n\nNo need to wait for write tasks to not defer deletion. This is because when entry is removed from the hot cache, we already wait for all write tasks. In the patch **0005** that I shared, I simply deleted files synchronously. It was `0.361719 ms` for 32 files.\n\nDeferred deletion may be required if hot cache will be decoupled from write tasks.\n\nBut I\u0027m **not suggested to remove** the deferred deletion.\n\nI suggest to remove tracking:\n```// Track that we\u0027re creating a pending task for this entry\n{\n    // Synchronize access to deferred task status\n    std::lock_guard\u003cstd::mutex\u003e lock(mDeferredTaskStatusMutex);\n    // Include buffer to handle the case when multiple tasks are pending for an entry\n    mDeferredTasks.insert(std::make_pair(entryHash, buffer));\n}\n```\n\nSo in order to delete blob you only need to:\n- remove from `mHotCache` (wait for write tasks if needed).\n- remove from `mEntries` and `mEntryStats`.\n- decrease cache size.\n- remove file in the deferred task or synchronously.\n\nTracking of deletion task is not required.",
      "parentUuid": "cc208ef2_6829304a",
      "revId": "694bfc703e12caf62b348924c4c45f742ec66db6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
